# Allen Relation: STARTS / STARTED-BY
#
# STARTS: A and B begin at the same time, but A ends first.
#   A starts B  iff  A.start = B.start and A.end < B.end
#
# STARTED-BY: the symmetric inverse — B and A begin together, B ends first.
#   B started-by A  iff  B.start = A.start and B.end < A.end
#
# Legal patterns that trigger STARTS:
#   two obligations or periods beginning on the same effective date
#   "as from the same date, both X and Y shall apply"
#   a specific protocol starting when a broader agreement starts
#   "from the entry into force, both the main agreement and annex X apply"
#   concurrent commencement with different termination dates
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed3):
#   Fishing opportunities protocol [1990-05-03, 1992-05-02] STARTS
#   provisional application period [1990-05-03, broader_end].
#   Both begin on 3 May 1990; the fishing protocol ends first.

```catala
declaration scope AllenStarts:
  input interval_a_start content date   # start of the shorter period
  input interval_a_end content date     # end of the shorter period
  input interval_b_start content date   # start of the longer period
  input interval_b_end content date     # end of the longer period
  output is_starts content boolean      # A and B share start; A ends first
  output is_started_by content boolean  # A and B share start; B ends first
```

## STARTS

Both intervals share the same start date, but A ends before B.

```catala
scope AllenStarts:
  date round down
  definition is_starts equals
    (interval_a_start = interval_b_start) and
    (interval_a_end < interval_b_end)
```

## STARTED-BY

Both intervals share the same start date, but B ends before A.

```catala
scope AllenStarts:
  definition is_started_by equals
    (interval_b_start = interval_a_start) and
    (interval_b_end < interval_a_end)
```
